# Changelog — publishing a version

Two separate user requests. Do not combine them.

**Only bump the version after you gave the user the time to ship the finalized version.**

The app version (`wails.json` `info.productVersion`, `internal/version/version.go` `Number`) stays on the version being shipped until the user asks for the bump.

## 1. Finalize (user asks to publish / finalize)

1. Turn the current highest heading into `## vX.Y.Z – Short summary` (summary after the dash). That heading’s version is the one already in `wails.json` and `version.go`. Do not change those version strings.
2. **User-facing changelog:** prepend a new release object at the **top** of `whatsNewReleases` in `frontend/src/help/whatsNew.ts` for `vX.Y.Z`.
3. Stop. Do **not** add the next changelog heading and do **not** bump the version.
4. Tell the user to ship this version before the bump: commit the finalize, build (`release.sh` or `wails build`), create the git tag, and push the tag to GitHub. Wait for them to ask for the bump.

## 2. Bump (user asks after the build and tag)

Only after they confirm the finalized version is built and the tag is pushed.

1. Add a new empty heading at the **end** of `CHANGELOG.md` for the next **patch** version (`v0.3.8` → `v0.3.9`), unless the user names a different bump. Newer versions stay below older ones; new bullets stay at the end of that last section.
2. Set that new version string in:
   - `CHANGELOG.md` (the new empty heading only; leave the closed release as-is)
   - `wails.json` → `info.productVersion`
   - `internal/version/version.go` → `Number` (no `v` prefix)
3. Do not add a `whatsNew.ts` entry for the empty next version.

## Writing `whatsNew.ts` entries

Audience: someone who already drafts and signs contracts in the app, reading **Hilfe → Was ist neu**. Each item answers: what can they do now, or what is different the next time they do a familiar task?

- **Language:** German. Address the reader as „Sie“. Up to three short sentences. Pragmatic, not a pitch. Use a second or third sentence for a consequence, a limit, or where to set it. Do not pad.
- **Lead with the outcome.** Name the action (finden, speichern, drucken, filtern, bestätigen) and the place in the UI (Menü, Stammdaten, Vertragstabelle, Einstellungen → …) when they would not find it otherwise.
- **No empty praise.** Drop adjectives that only compliment the change („übersichtlich“, „flüssig“, „zuverlässig“, „hilfreich“, „im Alltag“) unless the same sentence states the concrete behavior. „funktioniert wieder“ without the symptom is not enough.
- **No internal motive as the payoff.** Do not end on „hilfreich beim Support“, „für Debugging“, or an implementation detail. If the only payoff is support, either state the user action (Protokoll speichern und per E-Mail schicken) or omit the item.
- **Bugfixes:** Say what the reader gets. Weak: „Prozessschritte werden zuverlässig übernommen.“ Use: „Ändern Sie den Prozessschritt, wird er beim Speichern mitgeschrieben.“
- **Renames:** A short line so they find the control under the new name. A further sentence only if the menu then offers a choice they would miss („CSV: aktuelle Ansicht oder alle Verträge“).
- **One topic per item.** Merge only when it is the same task. Skip visual chrome the reader does not act on.
- **Omit:** `CHORE`, `REFACTOR`, `TEST`, `CI`, internal renames, build/typecheck fixes, Cursor rules, repo-only docs, and edits to older „Was ist neu“ wording. Do not announce those as a new release item.
- **Summary:** one German line of what the release is for (may differ from the English CHANGELOG title). No filler.
- **Structure:** `version` (no `v` prefix), `summary`, `items` (`text`, optional `help`).
- **Help links:** Set optional `help` to a help article id from `frontend/src/help/catalog.ts` when a topic deserves deeper reading. Do not link an item to `whats-new` itself.
- **Source:** Translate and filter the closed `CHANGELOG.md` section for that version; do not copy English `TYPE:` prefixes into the UI text.

Example:

- Weak: „Versionsnummer steht in Metadaten und Fuß — hilfreich beim Support.“
- Use: „PDF-Exporte können im Fuß den Firmennamen der Bibliothek zeigen. Daneben steht die Programmversion, mit der das PDF erzeugt wurde.“
